e":"78","crc32":"a280eb6a","sha1":"dff23fdd12cf6ec284aff010da1dec51c13bc60b"}],"files_count":57,"item_last_updated":1674680327,"item_size":102047019,"metadata":{"identifier":"a_warning_to_travellers_TNA","title":"A Warning to Travellers (Five Pounds in Notes)","mediatype":"movies","collection":["british_gov_public_films","ephemera"],"subject":"balance of payments","description":"A stark warning to holiday makers not to take more than \u00a35 in notes abroad. Richard Massingham. only five pounds in notes were to be taken abroad. balance of payments crisis.","publicdate":"2005-10-10 00:22:22","addeddate":"2005-10-10 07:22:14","uploader":"florian@archive.org","sponsor":"Central Office of Information for HM Treasury","publisher":"Public Relationship Films","sound":"sound","color":"color","runtime":"1:03","credits":"Public Information Films","rights":"UK Crown Copyright","language":"english","coverage":"Great Britain","updatedate":"2005-10-10 00:24:29","updater":"nVIR","backup_location":"ia903600_10"},"reviews":[{"reviewbody":"It looked like rubber face man was beign TOLD to take only five pounds.  Was that a law or something?","reviewtitle":"Was that a law or something?","stars":"4","reviewer":"Mewster","createdate":"2006-11-23 02:47:01","reviewdate":"2006-11-23 02:47:01"},{"reviewbody":"Yes, it was a law in England at the time.  Many countries still have very sharp limits on how much local currency can be taken out of (or into) the country.  The U.S. is one of the very few with no restrictions (other than to report amounts over $10,000) on how much you can take out or bring in.","reviewtitle":"The Law","reviewer":"Elvanion","reviewdate":"2008-01-01 20:59:49","createdate":"2008-01-01 20:59:49","stars":"2"},{"reviewbody":"5 Pounds in notes, get it!","reviewtitle":"A quick giggle","reviewer":"Framan","reviewdate":"2008-01-01 23:05:56","createdate":"2008-01-01 23:05:56","stars":"4"},{"reviewbody":"Somewhat odd and propagandish bit here admonishing travellers to ONLY bring five pounds in notes. Heaven forbid we'd have to pick you up from the airport when you spent all your money abroad. interesting piece of history here.","reviewtitle":"5.. POUNDS..","reviewer":"Spuzz","reviewdate":"2008-02-22 00:15:40","createdate":"2008-02-22 00:15:40","stars":"4"},{"reviewbody":"I wonder how long this rule was in effect? \nHow rigorous was this enforced and for what purpose was it for?\nI assume most Englishmen went to France or Spain for holiday, did the same hold true for those Countries?\nThis is a interesting piece of history. Was the Bank of England behind it ?","reviewtitle":"Very Interesting","reviewer":"Nikonwilly","reviewdate":"2010-01-24 02:17:13","createdate":"2010-01-24 02:17:13","stars":"4"},{"reviewbody":"The man's going abroad to watch \"dodgy\" cabarets, eat huge plates of shell fish while downing glass fulls of champagne.  Although really just propaganda, it's fun to watch propaganda.","reviewtitle":"Fun","reviewer":"skilpad","reviewdate":"2010-07-14 16:26:39","createdate":"2010-07-14 16:26:39","stars":"5"},{"reviewbody":"I was shocked to find out this has a listing on IMDb!","reviewtitle":"How very interesting","reviewer":"The_Emperor_Of_Television","reviewdate":"2012-03-27 09:29:53","createdate":"2012-03-27 09:29:53","stars":"5"}],"server":"dn601209.us.archive.org","simplelists":{"solo_manifest":{"solo_manifest_dn601209":{"sys_changed_by":{"source":"task","task_id":"5441746780"},"sys_last_changed":"2026-06-15 19:17:39.919582"}}},"solo":true,"uniq":557062859,"workable_servers":["dn601209.us.archive.org"]}